{number: 170}
{title: He Touched Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Shackled by a heavy burden,
'Neath a [G7] load of guilt and [C] shame;
Then the hand of Jesus touched me,
And now I am no [G7] longer the [C] same.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
He [G7] touched me, O He [C] touched me,
And [D7] O the joy that floods my [G7] soul!
Something [C] happened, and now I [F] know,
He [C] touched me and [G7] made me [C] whole.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Since I [C] met this blessed Savior,
Since He [G7] cleansed and made me [C] whole;
I will never cease to praise Him,
I'll shout it while e-[G7] ternity [C] rolls.
{end_of_verse}
